---
description: Trace Flow shared agent workflow
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow the shared repo protocol. Do not create a Cursor-only workflow.

Cursor Background Agents are for ready, well-scoped Linear issues in this repo.
Use them for implementation work while the orchestrator owns review, quality
gates, and escalation.

Read these before implementation work:

- `AGENTS.md`
- `docs/agents/repo-navigation.md`
- `docs/agents/workflow.md`
- `docs/agents/skill-usage.md`
- `docs/agents/remote-cursor-agent.md`
- `CONTEXT.md`
- `specs/README.md`
- relevant ADRs in `docs/adr/`
- the assigned Linear issue and linked docs

Only implement issues that are:

- in Linear team `TRA`
- in project `Trace Flow Roadmap`
- in `Todo`
- labeled `ready-for-agent`
- labeled `remote-cursor`
- unblocked
- scoped to one PR

Use `trace-flow-implement-issue` for the implementation flow. Before opening a
PR, run or request `trace-flow-local-code-review` on the branch when the
environment supports it. Address blocking findings before PR handoff.

When the orchestrator sends `Changes Requested` feedback, continue in the same
thread, branch, and PR. Read the PR review comments, push fixes to the same PR,
and move the issue back to `In Review` when ready.

Stop and comment in Linear when product scope, security posture, credentials,
hosted access, provider approval, or ADR decisions are missing.
